# isNodeJS Definition and Environment Detection Code

Here's the verbatim definition of `isNodeJS` with its surrounding comments:

```javascript
// NW.js / Electron is a browser context, but copies some Node.js objects; see
// http://docs.nwjs.io/en/latest/For%20Users/Advanced/JavaScript%20Contexts%20in%20NW.js/#access-nodejs-and-nwjs-api-in-browser-context
// https://www.electronjs.org/docs/api/process#processversionselectron-readonly
// https://www.electronjs.org/docs/api/process#processtype-readonly
const isNodeJS =
  (typeof PDFJSDev === "undefined" || PDFJSDev.test("GENERIC")) &&
  typeof process === "object" &&
  process + "" === "[object process]" &&
  !process.versions.nw &&
  !(process.versions.electron && process.type && process.type !== "browser");
```

This code detects a Node.js environment by verifying the existence of a `process` object with specific characteristics, while explicitly excluding NW.js and Electron contexts. The detection checks multiple conditions to distinguish genuine Node.js from browser environments that may have partial Node.js API compatibility.

